description: Stay on the current git branch; the user switches branches
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git branch

- Make all edits and commits on the **current branch**.
- Do not create a new branch (`git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git worktree add -b`) unless the user explicitly asks.
- If another branch is needed, tell the user and wait. They will switch.
- Do not rewrite history or force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
